+
+### Accepted-source canonical rebuild
+
+`--kvmem-recovery-mib N` enables a separate, positive source preparation byte quota, requiring `--kvmem-source-mib`. Both default off. The in-tree Engine API exposes `historical_sources()` and `prepare_source_rebuild(receipt, prefix_tokens, output_reserve_tokens)`. Submit the resulting raw-token prompt normally to reserve model resources and execute a fresh domain. This API neither restores exact old sparse/recurrent state nor migrates a source between Programs/models. It requires the entire canonical prefix and independently rounded output/draft headroom to fit; chunking is no capacity substitute.
+
+The source is copied under the recovery quota, and the ordinary prepared-input vector remains separate bounded request workspace. Source branching incurs a further S copy. Receipts are process-local and revision-sensitive; old derived windows may already be gone. Admission and each prefill/commit boundary revalidate the receipt. No old derived KV is used. Incomplete rebuilds are not retained as reusable histories; a successful whole commit closes preparation, returns its quota and allows normal new-domain retention. The HTTP completion schemas do not yet expose this in-tree API.
+
+Every `GenerationResult::accepted_source` names that request's actual captured source revision, independently of later queued requests. `historical_sources()` includes explicit branch ancestry. A receipt is source provenance, not proof that its model computation completed or that any derived KV remains resident.
